{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106171-thousand-years-of-night-errata-thread","id":1106171,"title":"Thousand Years of Night errata thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-21T11:32:35-07:00","id":1106171,"title":"Thousand Years of Night errata thread","content":"<a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/214130?affiliate_id=13&amp;src=TheOnyxPath\" target=\"_blank\">The advance PDF is out!</a> Please report any typos or visual glitches here. Discussion of setting, rules, and other content should go to other threads. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T13:21:41-07:00","id":1106227,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 120: </b>&quot;...learned a new ability from the experiments of the <b>Dragon his </b>torpor dreams.&quot; -- missing an <i>in</i><br /> <br /> <b>p. 135: </b>The &quot;<b>Prerequisite:</b> -&quot; line under &quot;Beast's Bargain&quot; seems to be an artifact of when this might've been a Merit. It's not needed for Conditions.<br /> <br /> <b>p. 135: &quot;</b>Your character created a revenant. The childe has a <b>-4 Blood Sympathy </b>to your character, <b>higher </b>than other revenants, and follows him wherever he goes.&quot; -- A negative number doesn't jive with a high Blood Sympathy. The sidebar on page 94 of VtR2nd has it that revenants gain +5 dice on Blood Sympathy to their sires. This should be +6? Or is something else meant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T13:26:54-07:00","id":1106228,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 29:</b> &quot;He can\u2019t replace a dramatically failed action, but if he can spend more than one Vitae in a turn, he can use the previous active effect to turn the dramatic failure into a normal one first and then replace it.&quot; -- There is nothing about the previous active effect (which adds to weapon damage ratings) that could possibly turn a dramatic failure into a failure, so I'm not sure what this is saying...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T13:30:40-07:00","id":1106231,"title":"","content":"This are minor nitpicks and might be me being anal about things but<br /> 1. How is Ezekiel of Sodom Akhud with no dots in prastentia<br /> 2. Only stated elder with disciplines above 5 is 200 year old draugr(Celerity 7). Wut?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T13:34:04-07:00","id":1106233,"title":"","content":"<b>Pg. 30: </b>&quot;The lower the character\u2019s Humanity drops, the more blatantly antagonistic the Ka becomes, and the stronger its urge to merge with the vampire grows.&quot; This seems to describe the opposite of what is in the table - higher Humanity allows the Ka to appear more often before granting Beats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T14:17:52-07:00","id":1106255,"title":"","content":"The Draugr Jack on <b>pages 112-113</b> has the following inconsistencies:<br /> <b>Survival 8</b> despite having Blood Potency 7 and most likely not having been in Torpor.<br /> <b>Celerity 7</b> despite Disciplines being limited to 5.<br /> <b>Health 7</b> despite having Size 5, Stamina 4, and Resilience 3. (Should be 9 or 12 depending on if Resilience is included in Stamina.)<br /> <b>Speed 6</b> despite having Strength 7, Dexterity 5, Size 5. (Should be 17.)<br /> <b>Initiative 4</b> despite having Wits 5 and Composure 2. (Should be 7.)<br /> <b>Defense 7</b> despite having Wits 5, Dexterity 5, Athletics 5 and Celerity 7. (Should be 15. Or 17 if you're not changing his literally impossible Celerity score.)<br /> Lacks the trait <b>Clan</b>.<br /> Additionally, his text implies he's mostly hunting humans rather than vampires despite Blood Potency 7.<br /> <br /> Jack the Draugr is a complete and total trainwreck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 06-23-2017, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T14:21:53-07:00","id":1106257,"title":"","content":"Using PDF pages.<br /> <br /> P4, 'muckity-muck' should be 'muckety-muck'<br /> P83, Major Domo should be one word, Majordomo<br /> P106, the term Garou is used, but that's not one Chronicles uses. 'a gang of Uratha' fits, 'a gang of werewolves' would fit too.<br /> P118, 'descendent' should be 'descendant' as it is spelled on other pages<br /> P128, it says 'Kitama' when it should say 'Kitamba'<br /> <br /> Ezekiel of Sodom, p116, should have at least one dot in Praestantia. As it's described every member of the Akhud has it.<br /> Jack on p112 has 'Celerity 7,' which isn't a thing. If the physical discipline is uncapped by elderhood, the book doesn't seem to go into it. Also, his Health should be 12. 5 to start, 4 from Stamina, and 3 from Resilience. His Speed should be 17, instead of 6. Speed = Size 5 + Strength 7 + Dexterity 5. His Initiative should be 7, and his Defense should be higher (Wits or Dexterity + Athletics + whatever his Celerity ends up being). His Survival should be 7, as it's capped by Blood Potency, also 7.<br /> <br /> I suppose a lot is going to depend on how the Physical Disciplines factor into the character stats. Bethenelle, on p113-114, should have 6 Willpower, and 5 Defense. Her Health, at 8, is correct based on her Stamina but her Resilience would up her Stamina by 2, giving her 10 Health. Unless this is already factored in, and her 'natural' Stamina is 1.<br /> <br /> Melina on p115 should have Speed at 14. Her Initiative should be 7, and her Defense 12 (if you're factoring in her Celerity, if not, 8).<br /> <br /> Ann Harlow, p115, should have Health 14 (that's counting Resilience 3). Her Willpower should be 8, Speed 16, and Defense 14 (if you're factoring in her Celerity, if not, 11).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-21-2017, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T15:40:06-07:00","id":1106296,"title":"","content":"Page 118: Is Priscus's touchstone, Giatina Rossi, correctly named? Her last name suggests an Italian origin but her first name is... I don't think it's actually a name. Maybe it was Giada? Or Giustina? (that's an old person name, but nowhere it is said that the youngest descendant of an ancient vampire should be young)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Italian nuisance. English is my second language, so be patient!<br /> <br /> <b>My homebrew:</b><br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/270766-domain-light-from-a-dead-star-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">[VtR 2e] Light From a Dead Star: Rome</span></a></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117941-hunting-ground-the-past-is-another-country-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>[WtF 2e] The Past Is Another Country: Rome</b></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3765-snesferatu","name":"SNESferatu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3765_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T15:56:23-07:00","id":1106300,"title":"","content":"Page 128. The Deadman\u2019s Reprieve talks about spending blood points instead of vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T16:48:47-07:00","id":1106322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106171-thousand-years-of-night-errata-thread?p=1106233#post1106233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Pg. 30: </b>&quot;The lower the character\u2019s Humanity drops, the more blatantly antagonistic the Ka becomes, and the stronger its urge to merge with the vampire grows.&quot; This seems to describe the opposite of what is in the table - higher Humanity allows the Ka to appear more often before granting Beats.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>think </i>the idea is that if it shows up a certain number of prescribed times you get a Beat. So at Humanity 9/10, it has to show up almost every scene before it yields a Beat (because it's a Rank 1 ghost and it can hardly do anything), whereas if you're at Humanity 2, if your Rank 5 monster of a doppelganger shows up even once, you're going to get a Beat.<br /> <br /> I might be wrong though. The wording is a little ambiguous.<br /> <br /> Edit: Reading the &quot;Frequency Before Beats&quot; section again, I'm actually not sure if that's what's intended. It might help to define Frequency Before Beats, or use a different phrase. Unless Charlaquin is right, but I think the table isn't talking about how often it shows up, just how often you get Beats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 06-21-2017, 10:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T16:56:09-07:00","id":1106326,"title":"","content":"<b>Bookmarks: </b>The bookmarks for the front and back cover are both labelled &quot;blank page.&quot;<br /> <b>p. 125: </b>Deborah has two Virtues, but she doesn't have the Virtuous Merit from the Chronicles of Darkness Rulebook. (Her Virtues/Vice are also First Edition style Heavenly Virtues / Deadly Sins, but that might be intentional considering her character).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 06-21-2017, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T17:23:06-07:00","id":1106335,"title":"","content":"Page 125: Deborah also has 11 Willpower, when the maximum willpower a character can have is 10.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T17:49:12-07:00","id":1106345,"title":"","content":"The <b>Married By Blood</b> merit (p83) has parts which don't make logical sense. For example, a vampire and their vampire spouse are already capable of sharing Haven dots without an additional merit. It also references &quot;Expenditures&quot; from a &quot;communal pool&quot; but there's no mention of the Resources merit. I get the sharing Retainers part (it's a nice EXP save, sort of), but the rest of the benefits seem wonky. What exactly is the merit meant to do? Was that meant to be Herd and Resources rather than Haven and Retainer?<br /> <br /> Also, loss of Status - Status they both have (ie, if they're both in the same City or Covenant), or all Statuses?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">The Yozis are right (and you should suffer and obey for all eternity).</span></b>","edited":{"userid":1487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1487-zahaqiel","user":"Zahaqiel","date":". 06-21-2017, 09:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1487-zahaqiel","name":"Zahaqiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T18:43:51-07:00","id":1106356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106171-thousand-years-of-night-errata-thread?p=1106335#post1106335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 125: Deborah also has 11 Willpower, when the maximum willpower a character can have is 10.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only ephemeral entities are explicitly limited to max 10 Willpower dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T18:56:12-07:00","id":1106361,"title":"","content":"page 20 - the architect Arc package is only worth 35 experience<br /> page 21 - the entertainer Arc package is only worth 35 experience<br /> - the puppet master Arc package is only worth 33 experience<br /> page 23 - the scholar arc package is worth 36 not 35 experience<br /> - the Shepard Arc package is worth 34 experience","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T19:21:07-07:00","id":1106378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106171-thousand-years-of-night-errata-thread?p=1106356#post1106356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only ephemeral entities are explicitly limited to max 10 Willpower dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>I stand corrected and apologize for my mistaken assumption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T19:43:19-07:00","id":1106384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WelshBoi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106171-thousand-years-of-night-errata-thread?p=1106361#post1106361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- the Shepard Arc package is worth 34 experience</div> </div> </div> </div>You sure?<br /> <br /> 4 Attribute dots, 16 Experiences.<br /> 5 Skills, 10 Experiences.<br /> Merits equal 7 Experiences. Bloodhound and Practiced Puppetteer are 2 a pop, the other 3 are 1 each.<br /> 2 Specialties for 2 Experiences.<br /> That's 35, right?<br /> <br /> It does say it costs 36, though. So the math on these should be double-checked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T19:43:59-07:00","id":1106385,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 76, Spontaneous Combustion:</b> The power says it's Contested but it's actually Resisted by Stamina. &quot;For each success rolled beyond the result of the victim\u2019s resistance roll,&quot; doesn't work because there's no roll listed. (By convention, it should be Resisted, since successes matter).<br /> <br /> <b>p. 83, Around the Block: </b>The bold style is bleeding into the words&quot;At least one Skill at...&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>p. 84/85, Special Treat: </b>&quot;<b>Vampire the Requiem 2e</b>&quot; should be <b>Vampire: The Requiem Second Edition<br /> <br /> p. 85, Spectral Communion: </b>The references to the Conditions should be to the Appendix, rather than &quot;below&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>p. 116, Ezekiel's stat block:</b><br /> - <b>Merits: </b>Ezekiel has Haven, but he doesn't have the minimum Safe Place 1 prereq<br /> - <b>Disciplines:</b> Despite being an Akhud, he almost doesn't have any of his clan disciplines: he doesn't have any Praestantia or Obfuscate and only 2 dots of Celerity (conversely, his Ghoul does have Obfuscate); Praestantia would potentially change some of his derived stats with its Dex boost<br /> - <b>Devotions:</b> <b>Dominate </b>is listed as one of his Devotions<br /> - <b>Derived Traits:</b><br /> -- Willpower should be 16<br /> -- Speed should be 18 (inclusive of Vigor)<br /> -- Defense should be 14 (inclusive of Celerity)<br /> <br /> <b>p. 116, Elizabeth Whateley's stat block:</b><br /> - <b>Skills:</b><b> Brawling </b>should be Brawl<br /> - <b>Skills: </b>She has a Stealth Specialty in Obfuscate, but no tiers of Obfuscate require that Skill to be rolled (it should be Larceny for Obfuscate 2)<br /> - <b>Disciplines: </b>She doesn't have Praestantia or Celerity, despite being an Akhud ghoul (though that could be intentional)<br /> - <b>Merits:</b> It doesn't say what levels of <b>Parkour </b>or <b>Trained Observer</b> she has<br /> - She's got Blood Potency 3, but she's a Ghoul and shouldn't have Blood Potency at all<br /> - Speed should be 16 (inclusive of Vigor)<br /> - Her armor rating is wrong; as per VtR2e, Kevlar is 1/3 armor<br /> <br /> <b>p. 117-118: </b>It's a small thing, but Priscus and Patrizia don't reflect that the Julii now have Vigor in-Clan, instead of Animalism (particularly Patrizia)<br /> <br /> <b>p. 118: Priscus' stat block:</b><br /> - <b>Merits: </b>He has Friends in High Places, but he has no Invictus Status, which means he can't use it.-<br /> <b>- Derived Traits</b>:<br /> -- Health should be 12 (that includes Resilience)<br /> -- Willpower should be 10<br /> -- Speed should be 15<br /> -- Initiative should be 11<br /> -- Defense should be 10<br /> <br /> <b>p. 118: Patrizia's stat block:</b><br /> - <b>Merits:</b> Sympathetic doesn't need the 2, as it only has a fixed dot rating<br /> <b>- Derived Traits</b>:<br /> -- Health should be 11 (that includes Resilience)<br /> -- Willpower should be 11<br /> -- Speed should be 12<br /> -- Initiative should be 10<br /> -- Defense should be 8<br /> <br /> <b>p. 120, Vlastislav's stat block:</b><br /> - <b>Merits: </b>He has Contacts 3, but only one Contact (City Hall) is listed; he should have two more<br /> - &quot;Unnatural Affinity Merit&quot; -- The word Merit is extraneous; Unnatural Affinity should be ranked between 1 to 5, and it should say what supernatural beings he can feed from.<br /> <b>Derived Traits: </b><br /> - Health should be 13 (inclusive of Resilience)<br /> - Speed should be 13 (inclusive of Vigor)<br /> - Defense should be 9 (inclusive of Celerity)<br /> - Also, there might not be room for this, but in the fluff text it says he can turn into sentient blood, but it doesn't have mechanics, here or in the main Pijavica write up earlier in the book<br /> <br /> <b>p. 120, Kin Ma</b><b>ker Devotion: </b>It doesn't include a Discipline in its activation roll; it should add Dominate<br /> <br /> <b>Back cover (ii): </b>The formatting on the last two bullet points is a bit off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 06-22-2017, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T06:29:46-07:00","id":1106514,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 29:</b> The Praestantia Discipline is worded very weirdly.<br /> The persistent effect adds the Praestantia dots to Dexterity when making rolls, which both implies that it does increase the attribute itself, and that it only gives bonus dice.<br /> It is described as specifically enhancing Initiative, which implies that it only gives bonus dice, but it is also mentioned as allowing Dexterity to be raised above the normal limits, which implies that it does increase the attribute.<br /> Clarification is needed.<br /> <br /> <b>p.83:</b> The new Merits are folded in under Elder Mysteries of the Dragon, both in the Bookmarks, and the actual text.<br /> <br /> <b>p.131-134: </b>There is no crossover info about Werewolf: the Forsaken or Hunter: the Vigil","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T08:10:14-07:00","id":1106557,"title":"","content":"So it doesn't get lost (I spoke to Danielle about it in Developer back-channel)<br /> <br /> The Mage crossover says mages can't use Mana to heal themselves like vampires use Vitae.<br /> <br /> Yes they can. It's called Pattern Restoration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T11:05:48-07:00","id":1106647,"title":"","content":"King Kitamba has a devotion that requires a dot of Obfuscate, but he doesn't have the first dot of Obfuscate. Was that intended, or?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T11:41:16-07:00","id":1106664,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 114: Bethenelle's stat block:</b><br /> - Health should be 10 (inclusive of Resilience)<br /> - Willpower should be 6<br /> - Defense should be 5<br /> <br /> <b>p. 114: Melina's stat block:</b><br /> - Speed should be 18 (inclusive of Vigor)<br /> - Initiative should be 7<br /> - Defense should be 12 (inclusive of Celerity)<br /> <br /> <b>p. 115: Ann Harlow's stat block:</b><br /> - Health should be 14 (inclusive of Resilience)<br /> - Willpower should be 8<br /> - Speed should be 16<br /> - Defense should be 14 (inclusive of Celerity)<br /> <br /> <b>p. 122: Rosamund's stat block:</b><br /> - Health should be 15 (inclusive of Resilience)<br /> <br /> <b>p. 123: Doyle's stat block:</b><br /> - Defense should be 9 (inclusive of Celerity)<br /> <br /> <b>p. 125: Deborah's stat block:</b><br /> - Speed should be 21 (unless I'm missing something; I can't find that last 6 points she's got)<br /> <br /> <b>p. 128: Kitamba's stat block:</b><br /> - He doesn't have Obfuscate but his Devotion is keyed off it<br /> - Health should be 14 (inclusive of Resilience)<br /> <br /> <b>p. 128: Deadman's Reprieve Devotion: </b>Doesn't have an activation roll listed, but it has roll results; doesn't have an Action or a Cost (&quot;Blood point&quot; should be Vitae, and it should be listed rather than be in the flavor text)<br /> <br /> <b>p. 130 Taxman's stat block:</b><br /> <b>Rituals: </b>The ritual &quot;Curse Vitae&quot; is listed as &quot;Cursed Vitae&quot; (but it might be that the ritual on the previous page is named wrong)<br /> <b>Derived Traits:</b><br /> - Health should be 8<br /> - Speed should be 15 (inclusive of Vigor)<br /> - Initiative should be 7<br /> - Defense should be 6<br /> <br /> <b>p. 125: </b>&quot;Cost&quot; under <b>Regeneration </b>is missing a tab","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 06-22-2017, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T12:20:58-07:00","id":1106688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106171-thousand-years-of-night-errata-thread?p=1106514#post1106514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>p.131-134: </b>There is no crossover info about Werewolf: the Forsaken or Hunter: the Vigil</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes there just isn't room. It's not realistic to expect another 1200 words of text are going to get added after the book's been laid out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T15:15:24-07:00","id":1106752,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>p. 19: </b>At the start of the page it notes that Blood Potency determines maximum ratings. But I believe 2nd edition states that higher ratings are kept when Blood Potency drops, so if a character has been in torpor, higher ratings should be possible depending on the maximum Blood Potency ever achieved.<br /> <br /> <b>p. 24-27: </b>The clan symbols in the background seem displaced to the wrong pages. Page 24 should be Daeva-Gangrel, page 25 should be Gangrel-Mekhet, page 26 should be Mekhet-Nosferatu, page 27 should be Nosferatu-Ventrue.<br /> <br /> <b>p. 29: </b>The last effect of Praestantia says that the previous effect can turn a dramatic failure into a normal failure, but the previous effect doesn't mention this at all.<br /> <br /> <b>p. 30: </b>There should not be a Carthian symbol in this page's background.<br /> <br /> <b>p. 85: </b>The two conditions mentioned under Spectral Communion are not &quot;below&quot;, but in the appendix.<br /> <br /> <b>p. 133: </b>Under &quot;Beasts in Game&quot; it says that a vampire can regain Vitae when a Beast regains Satiety. Shouldn't this be the other way around?</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T16:11:32-07:00","id":1106762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106171-thousand-years-of-night-errata-thread?p=1106688#post1106688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sometimes there just isn't room. It's not realistic to expect another 1200 words of text are going to get added after the book's been laid out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, true. But adding all but one of the other playable supers feels like they are deliberately shafted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T16:17:46-07:00","id":1106764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106171-thousand-years-of-night-errata-thread?p=1106762#post1106762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, true. But adding all but one of the other playable supers feels like they are deliberately shafted.</div> </div> </div> </div>They also forgot Mummy. You know, the gameline about ancient undead beings who cycle between periods of activity and unnatural rest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T17:47:39-07:00","id":1106802,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 116</b> Elizabeth Whateley stat block. Has the Merit Parkour, but does not list the dot rating. (It's a 1 - 5 dot merit)<br /> <b>p. 118</b> Priscus stat block. Has the Merit Closed Book, but does list the dot rating (It's a 1 - 5 dot merit)<br /> <b>p. 118</b> Patrizia stat block. Has the Merit Sympathetic listed as 2, which is correct, but other merits across the book that do not have a variable rating don't list the merit dot cost.<br /> <b>p. 120</b> Vlastislav stat block. Has the Merit Contacts (City Hall) 3. Contacts is a 1 dot merit.<br /> <b>p. 120</b> Vlastislav stat block. Has the Merit Cult Status (High Ritualist) 3. Cult Status doesn't appear to be a merit. Status is presented as Status (Organization) in the rest of the book. Or maybe the Merit is meant to be Mystery Cult Initiation? Unclear due to inconsistent format.<br /> <b>p. 120</b> Vlastislav stat block. Has the Merit &quot;Unnatural Affinity Merit,&quot; I think the Merit part is extraneous.<br /> <b>p. 125</b> <b>&amp;</b> <b>126</b> Deborah and Asher &quot;Crusader&quot; Harel stat blocks. Notes section lists merits that are not found in Vampire the Requiem Second Edition, however in numerous other cases (p. 115, Omen Sensitivity, Relentless; p. 116 Eidetic Memory, Multilingual, Investigative Prodigy; p. 118 Closed Book; p.128, Martial Arts; maybe more) Merits not found in VtR are used without similar text. Probably good to either always call it out, or not bother, or mention it all in one block earlier in the chapter.<br /> <b>p. 128</b> King Kitamba stat block. Has the Merit Danger Sense listed as 2, which is correct, but other merits across the book that do not have a variable rating don't list the merit dot cost.<br /> <b>p. 128</b> King Kitamba stat block. Has the Merit Indomitable listed as 2, which is correct, but other merits across the book that do not have a variable rating don't list the merit dot cost.<br /> <b>p. 128</b> King Kitamba stat block. Has the Merit Multilingual 3, this is a 1 dot merit that can be purchased multiple times, each time granting 2 languages. On p. 125 in Deborah's stat block it's correctly listed as a separate purchase twice, each purchase granting two languages.<br /> <b>p. 128</b> King Kitamba stat block. Status (Government) 3 has an unneeded trailing comma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4270,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","user":"literatzi","date":".  Fixed name for p. 120, also noted that Cult Status isn't a merit that I can find. 06-22-2017, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T17:53:29-07:00","id":1106806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>literatzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106171-thousand-years-of-night-errata-thread?p=1106802#post1106802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>p. 116</b><br /> <b>p. 122</b> Roasmund, the Head stat block. Has the Merit Allies (Corporate) 3, Allies is a 1 dot merit.<br /> <b>p. 128 </b>King Kitamba stat block. Has the Merit Allies (FBI) 3, Allies is a 1 dot merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Allies is 1-5 (I just checked)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T18:09:17-07:00","id":1106814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106171-thousand-years-of-night-errata-thread?p=1106806#post1106806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Allies is 1-5 (I just checked)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! Man, I could have swore it was changed but looking over CoD and VtR you are correct. I feel like this is a Berenstain Bears moment.<br /> <br /> Edit: Ah hah! It's Contacts that works that way. Going to edit my stat block post to reflect that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4270,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","user":"literatzi","date":". 06-22-2017, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T18:20:28-07:00","id":1106817,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>p. 135</b> Beast's Bargain (Persistent) Has the text <b>Prerequisite:</b> -, which appears to be unnecessary.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><br /> These are more nitpicky than anything but probably good to follow the formatting established across the edition.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>p. 136</b> Imprisoned Echo, missing &quot;</span></span><b>Beat:</b><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> n/a&quot; text which is present across all non-persistent Conditions in the game line.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>p. 137</b> Quiet Echo, missing &quot;</span></span></span><b>Beat:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> n/a&quot; text which is present across all non-persistent Conditions in the game line.</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>p. 137</b> Synchronized, missing &quot;</span></span></span><b>Beat:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> n/a&quot; text which is present across all non-persistent Conditions in the game line.</span></span></span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T19:28:47-07:00","id":1106834,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 110</b> Creating Inamorata &quot;All Inamorata receive the Enticing Merit for free.&quot; I'm not sure how they use the Enticing merit?<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire: the Requiem, Second Edition p. 92</b><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#262626\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Mortals can fight the Beast, but they cannot impose a Condition on the vampire. They do gain the +2 die bonus to attack, flee, or otherwise neutralize the risk.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>I'd love to hear someone else chime in.<br /> <br /> <b>p. 111</b> Daniel Howell stat block, has Humanity 8, presumably this should be Integrity 8 since Inamorata are statted like mortals.<br /> <br /> I have no idea how Elizabeth Whateley is supposed to work. I see what they're going for, but since nothing in the text explains or supports this I don't know what's an error and what isn't.<br /> <br /> <b>p. 116</b> Elizabeth Whateley stat block, has Blood Potency. Not sure if this is a mistake but nothing indicates why or how this is possible. Assuming it's just due to potent blood, and maybe it'll be expanded on in Half-Damned.<br /> <b>p. 116</b> Elizabeth Whateley stat block, has Humanity instead of Integrity. Not sure if this is intentional since she has Blood Potency.<br /> <b>p. 116</b> Elizabeth Whateley stat block, has text &quot;Touchstone: &quot;, if she has Humanity 6 she should probably have a Touchstone listed, or it should say &quot;None.&quot; If she should have Integrity, then the line can be removed.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T20:38:59-07:00","id":1106852,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 24 - 27</b> Clan Symbols behind text. Mekhet symbol appears on p. 24 but text is about Gangrel. Mekhet and Nosferatu symbol appear on p. 25, but text is about Gangrel and Mekhet. Ventrue Symbol appears perfectly, behind Nosferatu text on p. 26, no Ventrue text is on p. 26. Not sure if this is an issue, but it seems like the text moved around a bit and this was missed in layout.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T21:24:13-07:00","id":1106869,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Merit Qualification / More Merit stuff Pass</b></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>p. 116 </b>Ezekiel of Sodom stat block. Has the Haven Merit, but does not have the required Safe Place merit.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>p. 116</b> Elizabeth Whatley stat block. Has Fast-Talking 3, but does not have the required Subterfuge 2.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>p. 116</b> Elizabeth Whatley stat block. Has &quot;Fast Talk 3&quot; listed, this should be &quot;Fast-Talking 3.&quot;</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>p. 118</b> Priscus stat block. Has Friends in High Places merit, lacks required Status (Invictus) 1.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>p. 118</b> Priscus stat block. Has Practiced Puppeteer, this merit only applies to a single discipline, Dominate is the only one that meets the pre-reqs but maybe nice to note this?</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>p. 120</b> Vlastislav stat block. Has the Unnatural Affinity merit, no rating is listed (It's rated 1 - 5). Additionally each dot</span></span> allows a character to gain sustenance from one type of supernatural creature, the type(s) of creatures <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Vlastislav can feed from should be listed.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>p. 126</b> Asher &quot;Crusader&quot; Harel stat block. Has the Iron Will merit, but does not have the required Resolve 4.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>p. 128</b> King Kitamba stat block. Has the Merit Staff 5, should list the types of staff or skills the Staff is able to use.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>p. 130</b> Zach Wilson stat block. Has the Acute Senses Merit, but does not have a Blood Potency score, so the merit offers limited benefits. Not sure if this was intentional or not.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>p. 130</b> Zach Wilson stat block. Has the Iron Will merit, but does not have the required Resolve 4. Is this from his Mystery Cult initiation?</span></span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T22:36:36-07:00","id":1106886,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 29:</b> &quot;Celerity, <i>Praestantia</i>, Obfuscate&quot; should be &quot;Celerity, Obfuscate, <i>Praestantia</i>&quot;<br /> <b>p. 30: </b>Maybe clarification needed: Does the Julii bane apply to Blood Potency? I'm not sure if it's a Resistance Trait for the purposes of this bane. Also, does it cap dice pools, or just each individual trait?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 06-23-2017, 01:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T13:05:12-07:00","id":1107098,"title":"","content":"I don't know if it's an errata, but the Arcs seem awfully expensive in terms of experiences. Only Urban Legends or Methuselah can even buy most of them. They do not grant any disciplines. I think, they are a very good idea, but rather expensive and for younger elders not really feasible options. Is there any way to adress this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T13:24:09-07:00","id":1107406,"title":"","content":"P.130 - Zach Wilson -Story Notes<br /> <br /> &quot;As a young accountant, he <i><b>feels</b></i> in with Capone and even took a little off the top...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Feels&quot; should be &quot;fell&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T18:12:20-07:00","id":1107463,"title":"","content":"Page 59- Survival-Resolution and Moving On<br /> &quot;If the elder follows the Pitjantjatjara\u2019s lead and learns to respect the world, she gains dots in Survival, at least one dot in Humanity, and another in Fortitude.&quot;<br /> Fortitude isn't a thing in Requiem, as far as I'm aware. I think this was supposed to be Resilience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T18:18:08-07:00","id":1107465,"title":"","content":"Page 60- Triumph- Resolution and Moving On<br /> &quot;The competition rewards high physical-based Disciplines, such as Vigor and Fortitude. &quot;<br /> I believe that Fortitude isn't a discipline in Requiem, so this is probably supposed to be Resilience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T20:31:44-07:00","id":1107502,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 12: </b>&quot;...that devil\u2019s bargain elders strike so they can <b>to </b>rule and rest in turn.&quot; -- cut <i>to</i><br /> <b>p. 19: </b>&quot;The Merits in <b>the </b>Vampire: The Requiem Second Edition are as valuable...&quot; -- cut <i>the</i><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 06-25-2017, 12:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T21:58:35-07:00","id":1107511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WelshBoi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106171-thousand-years-of-night-errata-thread?p=1106361#post1106361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">page 20 - the architect Arc package is only worth 35 experience<br /> page 21 - the entertainer Arc package is only worth 35 experience<br /> - the puppet master Arc package is only worth 33 experience<br /> page 23 - the scholar arc package is worth 36 not 35 experience<br /> - the Shepard Arc package is worth 34 experience</div> </div> </div> </div>The Architect is correct as printed -- <i><b>Archeologist </b></i>is actually 35 where it's printed as 36, so that's the one that needs to change<br /> The Entertainer is correct as printed; it's 36 total (Barfly being a 2 dot Merit now is possibly the mistaken assumption here?)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T23:17:12-07:00","id":1108298,"title":"","content":"P. 102 - Revenants, paragraph 2.<br /> <br /> &quot;Revenants hold a dark mirror to elders. Revenants are cast out and hunted, whereas an elder is <i><b>surrounding</b></i> by bowing lackeys.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Surrounding&quot; should be &quot;surrounded.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T01:57:48-07:00","id":1108319,"title":"","content":"p. 104 - Barren Shores - Kindred:<br /> <br /> &quot;Kindred make great allies and enemies. They don\u2019t make Touchstones though.&quot;<br /> <br /> Should probably be:<br /> <br /> &quot;Kindred make great allies and enemies. They don\u2019t make <b>great</b> Touchstones though.&quot;<br /> <br /> This really confused me since I was looking specifically on whether they could be, and the first statement seemed to hint that they didn't - reading on cleared it up though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13616-nilaihah","name":"Nilaihah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T03:51:08-07:00","id":1108336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-of-Crows</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1106171-thousand-years-of-night-errata-thread?p=1107098#post1107098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if it's an errata, but the Arcs seem awfully expensive in terms of experiences. Only Urban Legends or Methuselah can even buy most of them. They do not grant any disciplines. I think, they are a very good idea, but rather expensive and for younger elders not really feasible options. Is there any way to adress this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Increasing the Experiences granted to a reasonable level instead of piggy-backing off of the numbers given in B&amp;S would work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T17:30:46-07:00","id":1108560,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 98: </b>Elders gain the Tainted Condition for diablerizing mortals, but Tainted's effects key off the victim's Blood Potency. Might be worth it to say Integrity is used instead? Or another Trait.<br /> p. 98: &quot;...he called the doorkeeper <b>\u201cbloke.\u201d</b> or that he...\u201d -- period is a typo","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 06-27-2017, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T17:42:24-07:00","id":1108568,"title":"","content":"<b>pg 98 - </b>I'm unclear about Mortal Souls. They're listed among the Touchstones, and the quote, &quot;Drinking a soul is an exhilarating experience that allows the Kindred to relive the mortal\u2019s life as she sucks out his soul: a beautiful and grisly reminder of what it\u2019s like to be human&quot; makes it sound like it's meant to be a possible Touchstone. But then later it says, &quot;A diablerized mortal can never serve as Touchstone.&quot; Is the intent here that the addiction becomes a Touchstone but the victims can't be? Or is it just a cool mechanic that doesn't provide a Touchstone in any way, and if so, why is it in the Touchstones section?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T21:07:46-07:00","id":1108615,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 76: </b>&quot;Such strength as Kindred of many centuries has exceeds the boundaries of his own flesh and bones...&quot; -- Kind of an awkward sentence, or there's a word missing; I think that needs rejiggering.<br /> <br /> <b>p. 99: </b>&quot;Her village depletes and the <b>Succubus </b>fights...&quot;<br /> <b>p. 99: </b>&quot;Love and happiness made the <b>Succubus </b>weak...&quot;<br /> <b>p. 103: </b>&quot;...reminds the <b>Succubus </b>of the desolation...&quot;<br /> <b>p. 106: </b>&quot;What the <b>Succubus </b>likes best...&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Succubus </b>should be &quot;Serpent&quot; as of Second Edition.<br /> <br /> <b>p. 110:</b> &quot;Inamorata are angels created by the <b>God Machine</b>...&quot; -- should be <i>God-Machine</i><br /> <b>p. 110: </b>&quot;Inamorata are a subset of <b>Demons</b>...See more on <b>Demons </b>in the Crossovers section...&quot; -- should be <i>demons</i><br /> <br /> <b>p. 110:</b> &quot;Drinking the blood of an Inamorata causes the <b>effectiveness of the Kindred\u2019s Disciplines </b><b>to be reduced by half </b>while she is under her Inamorata\u2019s sway.&quot; -- It's a little unclear what this means (e.g., is it referring to successes?). Many Discipline levels don't have any direct numerical factor (like Obfuscate 1 and 3), as they just work without rolling, or they have a story effect rather than a mechanical one.<br /> <br /> <b>p. 111, Daniel Howell's stat block:</b><br /> <b>Merits: </b>He's got Enticing, which as mentioned above, might not work for a &quot;mortal&quot; character<br /> <br /> <b>pp. 111-123: </b>None of the example characters on these pages have Virtue/Vice or Mask/Dirge. Characters after that have them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 07-01-2017, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T19:45:58-07:00","id":1111512,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 29: </b>&quot;Add the vampire\u2019s dots in Praestantia to her Dexterity when making Attribute or Skill rolls...&quot; This might relate to a previous errata question about Praestantia: is it meant to figure into the Defense calculation (i.e., does your defense change if your Praestantia-boosted Dex makes your Wits lower?) Or is it worded specifically that way to mean it doesn't?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}